WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
You cannot reliably detect, investigate, or explain activity that you cannot observe.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.465
OT blind spots carry operational consequences because an unseen system may control

00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:10.000
equipment,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.965
provide operator visibility, or bridge a critical communication path.

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:15.965
Missing evidence delays decisions when time and safety matter.

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:19.940
Telemetry supports asset inventory by revealing devices, roles, protocols, peers,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.000
and dependencies.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Observation can identify undocumented or dormant assets returning to service,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
but it does not replace engineering records or physical verification.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.965
Devices that do not communicate during collection may remain invisible.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:36.250
During incident response, telemetry helps reconstruct timelines, accounts, sessions,

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.000
affected assets, commands, configuration changes, and process conditions.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Vulnerability teams can use observed reachability and asset criticality to prioritize

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.205
findings rather than treating every vulnerable product as equally exposed.

00:00:48.205 --> 00:00:50.180
Business continuity also benefits.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:55.000
Communication loss, failed collection, degraded redundancy, unusual process trends,

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.085
or inaccessible remote sites may indicate a cyber event, equipment failure,

00:00:58.085 --> 00:00:59.000
or network problem.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Shared evidence lets teams coordinate diagnosis and recovery.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.965
IT and OT telemetry overlap, but their emphasis differs.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:11.000
IT sources commonly focus on users, endpoints, cloud services, and business applications.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.255
OT telemetry adds controllers, industrial protocols, field communications, process values,

00:01:16.255 --> 00:01:20.000
engineering activity, and long-lived devices with limited native logging.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.910
More data is not automatically better.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:26.190
Useful telemetry is selected around operational questions, collected safely,

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.965
retained appropriately, and enriched with asset and process context.

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:33.000
The objective is enough trustworthy evidence to reduce uncertainty without burdening

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.000
sensitive systems or analysts with unmanaged noise.
